<title>USA: Sybron Int'l to buy microbiology company.</title>
<headline>Sybron Int'l to buy microbiology company.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sybron International Corp said on Friday it signed a definitive agreement to acquire Remel LP, a manufacturer and distributor of products used in microbiology laboratories.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not announced.</p>
<p>Sybron said the deal, which is expected to close by the end of April, is a strategic fit for its Erie Scientific division because it adds a line of products that complement Erie's clinical business.</p>
<p>Remel posted annual sales of $60 million, Sybron said.</p>
<p>Sybron markets laboratory and dental supply products.</p>
<p>Its shares closed up 1/4 at 29-3/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
